---
import '../styles/site.css';
import Catalog from '../components/Catalog';
import AccessForm from '../components/AccessForm';
import DocumentDiagram from '../components/DocumentDiagram.astro';
import publicCatalog from '../../public/data/catalog.json';
const stats = publicCatalog.stats;
const snapshotDate = new Date(publicCatalog.generated_at).toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { day: '2-digit', month: 'long', year: 'numeric', timeZone: 'America/Los_Angeles' }).toUpperCase();
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"/><meta name="description" content="Cadastre is an open, source-traceable reference project for identity documents across all 50 U.S. states and the District of Columbia. Explore public sources, geometry schemas, and the review process."/><meta name="theme-color" content="#ffffff"/><title>Cadastre — A source of reference.</title><link rel="canonical" href="https://cadastre.kenshikilabs.com/"/><meta property="og:title" content="Cadastre — A source of reference."/><meta property="og:description" content="51 jurisdictions. Traceable sources. Open methods. A reference foundation for document intelligence."/><meta property="og:type" content="website"/><meta property="og:url" content="https://cadastre.kenshikilabs.com/"/><link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"/></head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <header class="site-header shell"><a class="wordmark" href="/" aria-label="Cadastre home"><svg data-cadastre-diagram="independent" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 5h14v5H10v12h12v-9h5v14H5Z"/><path d="M15 15h12M21 9v12"/></svg><span>cadastre<span class="wordmark-dot">.</span></span></a><nav aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="#catalog">The catalog</a><a href="#method">Our method</a><a class="nav-github" href="https://github.com/Kenshiki-Labs/state-id-harvester">Open source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></nav><a class="header-access" href="#access">Request access <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></header>
    <main id="main">
      <section class="hero shell" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
        <div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow"><span class="live-dot"></span> AN OPEN REFERENCE INITIATIVE BY KENSHIKI LABS</p><h1 id="hero-title">A source<br/>of <span>reference.</span></h1><p class="hero-intro">Document intelligence starts with knowing what you’re looking at.</p><p class="hero-description">A traceable reference foundation for identity documents across all 51 U.S. jurisdictions. Public sources. Open methods. Evidence you can inspect.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href="#catalog">Explore the catalog <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/Kenshiki-Labs/state-id-harvester">View the code <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><div class="hero-footnote"><span class="open-mark" aria-hidden="true">↗</span><span>Open code & schemas.<br/><strong>Controlled access to restricted research materials.</strong></span></div></div>
        <DocumentDiagram/>
      </section>
      <div class="stats-strip"><div class="shell stats-inner"><div><strong>{stats.jurisdictions}</strong><span>Jurisdictions in scope</span></div><div><strong>{stats.sources}</strong><span>Source PDFs collected</span></div><div><strong>{stats.jurisdictions_with_sources}</strong><span>Jurisdictions with sources</span></div><div><strong>{stats.accepted_cohorts}</strong><span>Accepted cohorts <i>Review pending</i></span></div></div></div>
      <section class="catalog-section shell section-space" id="catalog" aria-labelledby="catalog-title"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">01 / THE CATALOG</p><h2 id="catalog-title">The whole map.<br/><span>Every gap visible.</span></h2></div><div class="section-heading-aside"><p>50 states and the District of Columbia. Explore the discovery sources behind the collection and see exactly where review stands.</p><a class="text-link" href="/data/catalog.json" download>Download the public index <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div><Catalog client:load/><noscript><p class="noscript-note">The searchable catalog requires JavaScript. <a href="/data/catalog.json">Download the complete public catalog as JSON.</a></p></noscript><div class="catalog-context"><span class="context-mark" aria-hidden="true">↳</span><p><strong>A transparent starting point.</strong> Source counts track discovery, not coverage of every active card design. Discovery jurisdiction, publishing jurisdiction, and depicted credentials may differ. Some sources are quarantined as irrelevant. No extracted cohort has been accepted for runtime verification.</p><span class="snapshot-label">COLLECTION SNAPSHOT<br/>{snapshotDate}</span></div></section>
      <section class="method-section surface-ink" id="method" aria-labelledby="method-title"><div class="shell section-space"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">02 / THE METHOD</p><h2 id="method-title">From a public source<br/>to a defensible reference.</h2></div><p class="method-intro">Extraction is the beginning. Provenance, explicit uncertainty, and review turn an image into evidence.</p></div><div class="method-grid"><article><span class="step-number">01</span><h3>Collect with context.</h3><p>Discover public agency documents. Record their source URLs, publishing jurisdiction, retrieval metadata, and cryptographic fingerprints.</p><div class="step-tag">SOURCE → HASH → MANIFEST</div></article><article><span class="step-number">02</span><h3>Extract without pretending.</h3><p>Preserve native images, text, vector references and their placements. Associate design-specific source statements and leave uncertain relationships for review.</p><div class="step-tag">EXTRACTION ≠ ACCEPTANCE</div></article><article><span class="step-number">03</span><h3>Review before reference.</h3><p>Review depicted jurisdiction, document family, design generation, and geometry. Keep uncertain observations out of accepted cohorts.</p><div class="step-tag">EVIDENCE → REVIEW → COHORT</div></article></div><div class="metrology-note"><span class="note-symbol" aria-hidden="true">⊞</span><div><h3>Evidence appropriate to every claim.</h3><p>Sourced topology and tested computations can be published directly. ID-1 normalization supplies nominal coordinates. A claimed measurement tolerance or detection rate needs its own supporting evidence; physical-card collection is not a prerequisite for publishing the reference catalog.</p></div><a href="/schemas/cohorts.schema.json" class="text-link">Inspect the schema <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div></section>
      <section class="foundation-section shell section-space" aria-labelledby="foundation-title"><div class="foundation-copy"><p class="eyebrow">OPEN FOUNDATIONS. RESPONSIBLE ACCESS.</p><h2 id="foundation-title">Built to be<br/>examined.</h2><p>Useful infrastructure should make its assumptions inspectable. Cadastre publishes its collection code, schema contracts, and source index. Materials that could enable document replication belong behind accountable access.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/Kenshiki-Labs/state-id-harvester">Explore the repository <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><div class="foundation-cards"><a href="/data/catalog.json"><span class="resource-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#123; &#125;</span><div><h3>Public source index</h3><p>Jurisdictions, citations, fingerprints, and coverage gaps.</p></div><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="/schemas/cohorts.schema.json"><span class="resource-icon" aria-hidden="true">⊞</span><div><h3>Reference schemas</h3><p>Explicit geometry, provenance, and review contracts.</p></div><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="https://github.com/Kenshiki-Labs/state-id-harvester"><span class="resource-icon" aria-hidden="true">⌘</span><div><h3>Open collection pipeline</h3><p>Reproducible jobs, extraction logic, and review tooling.</p></div><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
      <section class="access-section" id="access" aria-labelledby="access-title"><div class="shell access-layout section-space"><div class="access-copy"><p class="eyebrow">03 / RESEARCH ACCESS</p><h2 id="access-title">For the people<br/>building trust.</h2><p>Request access to restricted reference research for legitimate identity verification, public service, compliance, or academic work.</p><ol class="access-steps"><li><span>01</span><div><strong>Tell us who you are.</strong><p>Provide your organization’s identity and intended use.</p></div></li><li><span>02</span><div><strong>Demonstrate domain control.</strong><p>Your request returns a unique DNS TXT challenge.</p></div></li><li><span>03</span><div><strong>Complete organization review.</strong><p>Domain control alone does not establish eligibility or grant access.</p></div></li></ol><p class="access-privacy">Already have a request? <a href="/access">Manage your research access request</a>.</p><p class="access-privacy">Public code and the source index are available without an account. Access requests are governed by our <a href="/privacy">privacy notice</a> and <a href="/acceptable-use">acceptable use terms</a>.</p></div><AccessForm client:load/><noscript><p>JavaScript is required to submit a research access request.</p></noscript></div></section>
    </main>
    <footer class="site-footer shell"><div class="footer-top"><a class="wordmark" href="/">cadastre<span class="wordmark-dot">.</span></a><p>Reference begins with evidence.</p><a href="https://kenshikilabs.com">A Kenshiki Labs initiative <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><div class="footer-bottom"><p>© 2026 Kenshiki Labs. Public research infrastructure.</p><nav aria-label="Legal navigation"><a href="/acceptable-use">Acceptable use</a><a href="/privacy">Privacy</a><a href="https://github.com/Kenshiki-Labs/state-id-harvester">GitHub ↗</a></nav></div><p class="footer-disclaimer">Independent research project. Not affiliated with or endorsed by any issuing jurisdiction. Public specimens and source documents do not establish authenticity.</p></footer>
  </body>
</html>
